<title>JAPAN: Kobe Steel to issue unsecured floating rate bonds.</title>
<headline>Kobe Steel to issue unsecured floating rate bonds.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>BORROWER - Kobe Steel Ltd</p>
<p>LEAD MGR - Sanwa Securities</p>
<p>FISCAL AGENT - Sanwa Bank</p>
<p> TYPE     unsecured floating rate bonds</p>
<p> ISSUE NO   6	  AMT   10 bln yen</p>
<p>DENOMINATION OF BOND  100 million yen each</p>
<p> COUPON   6 months Libor plus 0.5 pct annum of the principal</p>
<p>	    amount of the bonds with maximum rates of:</p>
<p>	    1st year, 1.10 pct; 2nd year, 1.15 pct;</p>
<p>	    3rd year, 2.10 pct; 4th year, 2.40 pct</p>
<p>	    5th year, 3.25 pct and the last six months, 3.30 pct</p>
<p> ISS PRICE  100 yen   MATURITY 07.JUL.02</p>
<p> LAST MOODY'S	   PAY DATE 17.Jan.97  INT PAY 17th Jan/Jul</p>
<p> LAST S&amp;P		 SIGN DATE	     SUB DATE 24.Dec</p>
<p> LAST JCR AA-	   LAST JBRI	     LAST NIS</p>
</text>
